{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicDihedralAngle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicDihedralAngle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GeodesicFaceH3"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dihedralAngle_edgePerp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dihedralAngle_edgePerp","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L117-L133","doc":"**The workhorse.**  If the two interior edge-perpendicular in-face vectors are\nunit (base normals unit, signs `±1`) and their dot product is `cos θ` for some\n`θ ∈ [0, π]`, then the dihedral angle along that edge is `θ`.\n\nThis is genuinely non-vacuous: the dot product is the actual Euclidean dot of the\ntwo rotated normals, and `θ` is recovered as `arccos` of it — the standard\nmeasurement of a dihedral angle in the conformal model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dihedralAngle_eq_euclidean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dihedralAngle_eq_euclidean","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L109-L115","doc":"The hyperbolic dihedral angle equals the Euclidean angle between the two\nedge-perpendicular in-face tangent vectors (File 1, `z > 0`) — hence is\nheight-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dihedralAngle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dihedralAngle","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**The hyperbolic dihedral angle** along a common edge, between two\nedge-perpendicular in-face tangent vectors `e₁, e₂` at height `z`: the hyperbolic\nangle between them.  (For a vertical edge these are horizontal vectors; File 1\nmakes the value height-independent and equal to the Euclidean angle.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inner_edgePerp_normal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inner_edgePerp_normal","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L93-L98","doc":"**The dot product of an `edgePerp` vector with a neighbour's base normal** —\nthe quantity whose SIGN certifies the interior orientation (negative = points\ninto the neighbour's half-space, i.e. into the wedge). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inner_edgePerp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inner_edgePerp","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L87-L91","doc":"**The dot product of two `edgePerp` vectors.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inner_edgePerp_self_normal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inner_edgePerp_self_normal","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**`edgePerp n s` lies in its own face**: it is perpendicular to the face's\nbase normal `n` (dot product zero) — the \"in-face\" certificate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.norm_edgePerp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.norm_edgePerp","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**`edgePerp` is a unit vector** when the base normal is unit and `s = ±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.edgePerp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.edgePerp","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L65-L72","doc":"**The interior edge-perpendicular in-face tangent vector** of a vertical face\nwith base normal `n`, oriented by `s = ±1`.  It is the 90°-rotation\n`s·(−n.2, n.1)` of the normal: horizontal (so ⊥ the vertical edge), in the face\nplane (⊥ `n`, see `inner_edgePerp_self_normal`), and unit when `n` is unit and\n`s = ±1`.  The sign `s` is chosen (per wedge) so the vector points into the\nwedge, certified for a concrete wedge by `inner_edgePerp_normal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.norm2_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.norm2_one","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L56-L61","doc":"The norm of an explicit horizontal 2-vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inner2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inner2","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The inner product of two explicit horizontal 2-vectors is the dot product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.embN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.embN","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L49-L50","doc":"Embed a base direction `n : ℝ²` as a horizontal Euclidean 2-vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.v2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.v2","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicDihedralAngle.lean#L46-L47","doc":"An explicit horizontal Euclidean 2-vector. ","signatureChunk":0}]}